Cell["<< PhysicalConstants`", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f54a00e-6c79-4093-9c2e-f9a0f791f182"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\

Primis \
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"eda571d5-b013-41ed-9b78-a71764038725"],

Cell["\<\
Two States : (Existance | Null)
Existance defined as Not Null: The Set of All Properties

Existance cast shaddow / leaves hole in the Null (Plain)
Has all properties of Existance with - sign; equevelnt to hole in \
semiconductores
Hole has the inverse of any and all properites of existance but not the \
properity of existance: it is a shaddow of existance on the Null Plain. \
Existance requires Two Enities The Existance Enity (as defiend by any \
arberturally selected properity) and the Shaddow of The Existance Enity  (as \
defiend by the Conjugate of the arberturally selected properity: Note \
Mathematical Complex Conjugate)
\
\>", "Subsubtitle",ExpressionUUID->"00806c79-92b3-4a1e-ade7-3f7437f50162"],

Cell["\<\
At One Dimition there is One Phase formed by Existance and \
Conjugate[Existance]; {Existance | Conjugate[Existance]}; a Vector in a \
ComplexPlane.

{Existance | Conjugate[Existance]} pair are now addressed per the matholoty \
from Chapeer 5 and above of The Power Of Alpha by MacGregor. The mathematical \
implimentaion however will be quantified on a reflection count basis using \
matirx approch.          

\[OpenCurlyQuote]\[CloseCurlyQuote];;



\
\>", "Subsubtitle",ExpressionUUID->"3c612bb6-08d1-4398-8a01-e4c869f28cb0"],

Cell["\<\
The {Existance | Conjugate[Existance]} pare will be approched as a Spinor per \
the work of Cartan in The Theory of Spiniors. The The {Existance | \
Conjugate[Existance]} pair Plankette form the Priodial \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]Partical\[CloseCurlyQuote]




\
\>", "Subsubtitle",ExpressionUUID->"265e2153-138c-4f17-9794-a7428468051c"],

Cell["\<\


Phase comes 1
Dim comes second
Dim result of Phase Alinement
Phase Pure Complex entity
Where Phase alinges get vector in reals
A Vector defines a spacetime in Din N(n)
Phase =1 Dim 



\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7116141574204473`*^9, 3.711614171549252*^9}, {
   3.7116143893960123`*^9, 3.711614389643882*^9}, {3.711614437147675*^9, 
   3.711614450739368*^9}, {3.711614500875332*^9, 3.711614568354994*^9}, {
   3.711614946459784*^9, 3.7116152549491577`*^9}, {3.711615362423709*^9, 
   3.7116153653835583`*^9}, 3.711615538074534*^9, {3.7116156150672493`*^9, 
