Cell["\<\
The Progression
Maybe :
   Propertiy:
  \thave <Some-Thing>
\t\tIf look for <Some-Thing> ==== Will find <Some-Thing>
\t\t<Some-Thing> subset Unity
\t\t<Some-Thing> comes in quatum units
\t\tIm ==== have <Some-Thing>
  \t<Some-Thing> ==== Im 
  \t\thas the Sqrt[ neg one ] behavour set
  Assumtions:
  \t
  \tPair Production is {I and its Conjugate}
  \t\tAll Pair Production???
\tStarted with null
  \t\tNull ==== \[OpenCurlyQuote]no delta\[CloseCurlyQuote] aganst <everything>
  \t\tNull is {}; nullset 
  \tNull - I = -I + Null
  \t\tMust sum to Null appon condition of <Some-Thing>
  \tGet I get -I to balance to Null
  \tForces Pair Creation
  \t-I reflection I by definition
  \t-I == Conjugate[I]  \t
  \tPair {I,-I} column vector
  \t\tA Spinor
  \t\tComplex Doman
  \t\tBegets Two Matrix Cartan MatrixX and his \[OpenCurlyQuote]a prior \
Matrix\[CloseCurlyQuote]
  \t\tSingle Phase or Dimention.
  \t\t\tPhase maps to Dimention
  \t\t\tImplies Phase is Quantizied
  \t\t\t\tThe Count Properity?
  \t\t\t\tCount Placeholder for Phase for now
  \tAll reflections rotations (Cartan, Altway, etc)
  \t\tUsing MacGregor Power of Alpha Chapter 5 up
  \t\tGet Relitivist Spining Sphere in 
  \t\t\tColplex Doamin
  \t\t\tWith Generation of a Real Vector = {1};
  \t\t
  \t\t
  \t
 have neg I the ReflectionTransform\
\>", "Subsubsection",
